- **ID**: TASK-260720-34d4du
- **Title**: TASK-260720-34d4du: extend-reluxniossh-fork-for-adapter-conformance
- **Parent**: STORY-260715-lkshfz
### Description

Extend the ReluxNIOSSH minimal fork (TASK-260715-nzdzv3) with the three public API surfaces the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6) requires for the NIOSSH adapter (TASK-260715-1af33i), discovered during adapter integration (see TASK-260715-1af33i_fork-api-blocker.md). Keep concrete NIOSSH types inside the fork/adapter boundary; PRESERVE the security-preserving async-external-signer contract (private keys stay in Keychain, never exported). Extend the existing 16-file allowlist delta minimally; the growing delta is recorded evidence for the eventual engine selection (TASK-260715-1gjxer).
### Acceptance Criteria

1. Public external public-key signer auth offer: an async signature path accepting wire-format public key + algorithm and calling back for the signature over NIOSSH's constructed payload, WITHOUT requiring or exporting a concrete NIOSSHPrivateKey; a deterministic fork test proves auth succeeds via an external async signer. 2. Public reply-observing keepalive/global-request: send keepalive@openssh.com (or a generic global request) with want-reply, bounded payload, preserving NIOSSH packet ordering/encryption/MAC and request-response ordering, exposing reply completion for RTT; a fork test proves the request->reply round-trip. 3. Caller-configurable KEX and host-key allowlists PLUS a public immutable negotiated-algorithm snapshot/event reporting exact KEX, host key, cipher, MAC; a fork test proves the allowlist constrains negotiation and the snapshot reports actual negotiated values (not configured lists). 4. Added delta stays minimal + allowlisted, documented in PATCH_MANIFEST/delta doc; upstream crypto/algorithms unchanged; Apache-2.0 attribution preserved; the 323 upstream tests still pass. 5. swift build, the new fork tests, and make validate-core (no NIOSSH/SwiftNIO leak into ReluxTunnelCore) pass.

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### TASK-260720-34d4du_inputs.md
> Fork extension: 3 public API hooks

Extend the ReluxNIOSSH fork (Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH, pinned swift-nio-ssh 0.14.1/31cdc3c) with three PUBLIC API surfaces the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6, in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift) needs for the adapter, discovered by TASK-260715-1af33i (read TASK-260715-1af33i_fork-api-blocker.md for exact upstream line refs). (1) EXTERNAL ASYNC SIGNER: add a public public-key user-auth offer that takes wire-format public key bytes + algorithm and an async signature callback over NIOSSH's constructed auth payload, WITHOUT constructing/holding/exporting a concrete NIOSSHPrivateKey (upstream only offers Offer.privateKey with a concrete key + synchronous internal signing). Private keys must never leave the caller (security-privacy.md). (2) REPLY KEEPALIVE: expose a public reply-observing global-request op (the internal sendGlobalRequestMessage/GlobalRequestMessage) so the adapter can send keepalive@openssh.com with want-reply + bounded payload and measure RTT, preserving packet sequence/encryption/MAC ordering. Do NOT reuse sendTCPForwardingRequest (creates remote listeners). (3) ALGORITHM POLICY + SNAPSHOT: expose caller-configurable KEX + host-key allowlists on the client configuration AND a public immutable snapshot/event of the EXACT negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC (upstream keeps NegotiationResult + host-key accessor internal/test-only). Keep the delta MINIMAL and allowlisted, update PATCH_MANIFEST + delta/rebase docs, preserve Apache-2.0 attribution, keep upstream crypto untouched and the 323 upstream tests green, add deterministic fork tests for each hook. Concrete NIOSSH types stay inside the fork/adapter boundary (ReluxTunnelCore must not import them; make validate-core enforces). If any hook cannot be exposed without a large/unsafe change, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact delta + a viability note for TASK-260715-1gjxer.




